{"body":"Found while verifying #1398. Its repair stops KGX pooling only for the four Rhea node columns. Every other node column that the pinned model does not declare multivalued is still written as a pipe-joined pool of each declarer's value, blanks included. (#1398's fifth bullet, blank `xref` becoming `|`, reproduces only under the test fixture schema: the pinned model declares `xref` multivalued, and in the 2026-10-13 build no `xref` value has a blank or repeated token.)\n\nMechanism, at 1acb8b61f:\n- `_MULTIVALUED_NODE_PROPERTIES` comes from the pinned model (`kg_microbe/merge_utils/kgx_source.py:83-87`). `has attribute type` is `multivalued: false` there (`data/raw/biolink-model.yaml:418-423`), so `RelationAwareTsvSource.read_node` keeps it as a literal scalar (`kgx_source.py:316-318`).\n- KGX 2.7.0's `prepare_data_dict` treats a key missing from its own table as multivalued and appends every contribution without a membership check (`kgx/utils/kgx_utils.py:644-674`). Nodes pass through it in `merge_assertion_graphs` (`kgx_source.py:209`) and, for an ID repeated within one source, in `RelationAwareGraphSink.write_node` (`:364-369`).\n- `RelationAwareTsvSink.write_node` canonicalizes only `deprecated` (`:505`), the Rhea columns (`_canonical_rhea_node_scalar`, `:423-440`, applied at `:508-509`) and blank `description` items (`:510-515`, #1200). Any other list is joined with `|` (`:491-492`).\n\nEvidence:\n- A hermetic probe through `parse_source` -> `merge_assertion_graphs` -> `RelationAwareTsvSink` under the pinned 4.4.2 model, with two sources declaring one node: `has_attribute_type` blank+blank gives `|`, `X`+`X` gives `X|X`, `X`+blank gives `|X`, and `X`+`Y` gives `X|Y` with no error. The Rhea contract refuses that conflict.\n- In the 2026-10-13 build (1804424c0-dirty), 29 merged nodes have `has_attribute_type` exactly `|`. They are the 29 NCBITaxon IDs that both `data/transformed/bacdive/nodes.tsv` and `data/transformed/microbedecoder/nodes.tsv` declare, blank on both sides (e.g. NCBITaxon:1341). The other 22,796 values are single CURIEs, and the Rhea columns hold no pipes. No second source declares MicrobeDecoder's three `attribute_type_*` columns. Its 35 pipe-joined `attribute_type_evidence` values are its own text and pass through unchanged.\n- `tests/test_merge_node_descriptions.py:166` pins the current behaviour: a blank+blank custom node column must serialize as `|`.\n\nRelated node-merge defects in the same pass:\n- `description`: #1200 removed only blank contributions and kept repeats (`tests/test_merge_node_descriptions.py:79-80`, `:94`). In the 2026-10-13 build, 51,676 descriptions contain a pipe: 3 are FOODON source text, 16,976 repeat one identical text (e.g. CHEBI:113455 twice, CHEBI:15355 three times) and 34,697 join different source descriptions. Order-preserving deduplication of identical description items (`A|A` -> `A`) removes the 16,976 duplicates while preserving distinct descriptions from multiple sources.\n- `name`: KGX treats `name` as a core property (`kgx_utils.py:34`) and keeps the first declaration, even a blank one. In the 2026-10-13 build, 14 nodes have a blank merged name although a source named them (e.g. for `EC:1.7.2.1`, BacDive's blank declaration beat `\"nitrite reductase (NO-forming)\"` from EC and Rhea). Ignore blank `name` declarations when another source supplies a non-blank `name`.\n\nFix in `kg_microbe/merge_utils/kgx_source.py` (outside `SHARED_CODE` at `kg_microbe/utils/transform_fingerprint.py:43-55`, so no producer reruns are required):\n1. Generalize `_canonical_rhea_node_scalar` into a single scalar-column contract for every node column outside `_MULTIVALUED_NODE_PROPERTIES` (keeping the Rhea value checks): drop blank contributions, collapse identical ones, and refuse distinct non-blank values, naming the node ID and column. Apply it to the contribution list KGX built, never to pipe-split text.\n2. Deduplicate identical non-blank `description` items in order (`A|A` -> `A`) while keeping distinct source descriptions joined.\n3. Treat blank `name` values as absent during node merging so a non-blank `name` from any source wins over `\"\"`.\n\n**Acceptance:**\n- A `kgx_source` test: two sources declare one node with `has_attribute_type` blank/blank, `X`/`X`, `X`/blank and `X`/`Y` -> `''`, `X`, `X` and an error naming the node and column; `description` `A`/`A` -> `A` and `A`/`B` -> `A|B`; `name` `\"\"`/`\"foo\"` -> `\"foo\"`. Update `test_merge_node_descriptions.py` to match.\n- The next merge has no value in a single-valued node column other than `description` that is only pipes, starts or ends with `|`, or repeats a token, no repeated identical `description` items, and 0 blank `name` values where any source supplied a name.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","comments":[],"number":1674,"state":"OPEN","title":"Canonicalize single-valued node columns, deduplicate repeated descriptions, and ignore blank names at merge","url":"https://github.com/Knowledge-Graph-Hub/kg-microbe/issues/1674"}
